+{"body":"Ontology v9 (#816) breaks the IDD routing table. The table in `docs/philosophy/idd-principles.md` says: the builder never gets failure conditions; the eval author gets all of ICE. That principle must hold.\n\n## What breaks\n\n1. **The builder sees failure conditions.** In v9 a Story's scope of work says \"what must never happen\". The Story is a tracker issue, and the builder reads it. So the failure conditions reach the builder. This is the break.\n2. **The eval does not get all of ICE.** In v9 the eval reads only the epic, its stories and the usage guide, never the ICE. That part is fine as long as the plan play writes every part of the ICE it needs into what the eval reads. With break 1 fixed, the failure conditions must still reach the eval by some other path.\n3. **Recovery conditions have no home.** The validator needs them to build the recovery handoff. v9 does not say where they go.\n\n## What does not break\n\n- One interpretation of the ICE (the plan play writes it once) stays. The eval reads what the plan play wrote, not the raw ICE.\n- The eval is hidden from the builder (`plans/<plan-id>/evals/` is never read by a builder).\n\n## The fix (proposed)\n\nThe plan play splits what it writes from the ICE:\n- **On the Story (the builder reads it):** goal, constraints, expectations (success scenarios). No failure conditions.\n- **In the slice's eval folder** `.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slice>/` **(the builder never reads it):** the failure conditions and the recovery conditions for each story, written by the plan play.\n- The eval play reads the epic, the stories, that hidden file and the usage guide. So it gets all of the ICE, as the plan play interpreted it once.\n\nThis is an ontology change (Story, Slice), so it goes through /edit-ontology.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The ontology says the Story never carries failure or recovery conditions, and names the hidden file in the eval folder that holds them.\n- The routing table in `idd-principles.md` stays true, word for word, for the builder and the eval author.\n- The ADR (#824) records this.\n- Plan 788 does not land in plan/756/base before this is done.\n\nFound in the review of PR #823.\n","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORA56Ic8AAAACe8Vedg","name":"defect","description":"Defect report","color":"d73a4a"}],"number":826,"state":"OPEN","title":"Ontology v9 breaks the IDD routing table: keep failure conditions off the Story"}
